# Captured originals are addressed by the sha256 of their exact bytes, so git must
# store them byte for byte. Without this, a CRLF page fetched on Windows is normalised
# on the way in and its stored content no longer hashes to its own file name.
.scratch/**/evidence-*/** -text
.scratch/**/artifacts/sha256/** -text
.scratch/pring-data-acquisition-repair/credit-window-inputs-186/** -text
